# Ollama Modelfile: a coding agent model with a deliberately capped context.
#
# Build it:
#   ollama create qwen-coder-32k -f Modelfile
# Run it:
#   ollama run qwen-coder-32k
#
# Why 32768 and not the model's full 262144: instruction adherence degrades long
# before you hit the advertised ceiling, and a small window forces you to clean
# up instead of letting junk accumulate. See the article for the reasoning.

FROM qwen3.6:27b

# The whole point. Ollama's own default scales with your VRAM (32k on a 24-48 GiB
# card, 256k at 48 GiB or more), so depending on the box this line either raises a
# small ceiling or drags a huge one back down. Either way it pins the number.
PARAMETER num_ctx 32768

# Low temperature for code. Raise it if you want prose out of the same model.
PARAMETER temperature 0.2
PARAMETER top_p 0.9

# Deliberately absent: any KV cache quantization. That is configured through the
# OLLAMA_KV_CACHE_TYPE environment variable, not here, and for agentic work you
# want to leave it at the f16 default. Quantization errors in the cache compound
# across a long multi-turn session.

SYSTEM """
You are a coding agent working in an existing repository.

Read AGENTS.md before writing code and match the patterns it shows.

Work on exactly the task you were given. If you need a file you were not handed,
ask for it by path instead of searching the repository. Unrequested exploration
fills the context window with material that is mostly irrelevant to the task and
crowds out the instructions you were given.

When you are unsure about an API, say so and ask. Do not invent a function
signature that looks plausible.
"""
